# This is the human-edited intent file. Do not hand-edit requirements.txt;
# regenerate it instead (see the header comment in requirements.txt).
#
# The committed requirements.txt was resolved with pip-compile on Linux /
# CPython 3.11. Hashes cover every published wheel of each pinned version, so
# installs work cross-platform, but a dependency that only appears under a
# Windows environment marker would be missing from the lock. If a Windows
# `pip install --require-hashes` reports an unpinned requirement, re-run the
# pip-compile command from the requirements.txt header on Windows and commit
# the result.
